Z||000000||GodSend||08-23-2000||02:34 PM||||  I was flipping through the archive looking for warm start solutions when I came across a post from a few people who fixed the problem by replacing the 170-190 thermostat with the 160-180 thermostat.<P>  I went to a few Canadian Tires to try to pick it up, but It seems to be a hard piece to find (ill just order through the parts desk).  Can anyone comment on their experiance with this swap, and the reason it may work (can someone please explain the difference in the two.)<P> Thanks Alot.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||08-23-2000||04:20 PM||||The only 2 easily available replacement thermostats that I know of are the stock 195* and a 185* thermostat.  I replaced my 195 with the 185, and the temp stays pegged at the first 1/3 mark, which is exactly how I like it.  There's also a 160* thermostat, but you need to run a different chip because the ecm will think the engine is always cold, and therefore run too rich and you'll get worse performance and gas mileage.<P>Any place that carries Stant products should be able to get the 195* and 185* thermostats<P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 149,000 miles and counting!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||1
